      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The isolated CAN transceivers U10 and U11 have both GND1 and GND2 pins tied to the same common GND net.",
      "expected": "For an isolated CAN transceiver used to implement isolated CAN buses, GND1 and GND2 should be separate isolated ground domains, not shorted together.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND [High Power] : ... U10.4(GND1,power_in) U10.5(GND2,power_in) U11.4(GND1,power_in) U11.5(GND2,power_in) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The galvanic isolation of the CAN interfaces is defeated, making the buses behave as non-isolated CAN buses and exposing them to ground-loop and noise issues that the isolated design was intended to avoid.",
      "confidence": 0.66
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show at least two substantive deviations: an LED power net is left floating with only LED anodes attached, and the isolated CAN transceiver grounds are tied together, defeating the stated isolated CAN architecture."
}

